  "instructions": [
    "Preheat the oven to 375°F (190°C).",
    "Heat the olive oil in a large skillet over medium heat.",
    "Add the onion, garlic, carrots, and zucchini and cook until the vegetables are tender, about 10 minutes.",
    "Add the madras paste and cook for another minute, stirring constantly.",
    "Stir in the diced tomatoes, vegetarian ground beef substitute, oats, vegetable broth, nutritional yeast, salt, and black pepper.",
    "Bring the mixture to a simmer and let cook for 10 minutes, stirring occasionally.",
    "Transfer the mixture to a 9x13 inch baking dish and top with shredded vegan mozzarella cheese.",
    "Bake the casserole for 25-30 minutes, or until the cheese is melted and bubbly.",
    "While the casserole is baking, prepare the cashew sour cream by blending 1 cup of cashews with 1 tablespoon of lemon juice and 1/4 cup of water until smooth and creamy.",
    "Remove the casserole from the oven and top with a dollop of cashew sour cream and some chopped parsley and cilantro.",
    "Serve hot and enjoy!",
    "Cook ground beef to an internal temperature of 71°C / 160°F (no longer pink in the middle) before serving."
  ],
